Figure 1: Snapshot of a one-dimensional (1D) parallel shock with a non-relativistic upstream plasma flow of $u_{0}=0.4$. From top to bottom:
(a) ion phase-space diagram in $(x,U_{\mathrm{ion},x})$;
(b) electron phase-space diagram in $(x,U_{\mathrm{ele},x})$;
(c) plasma density (red);
(d) transverse magnetic fields $B_{y}$ (blue), $B_{z}$ (red), and their envelope $(B_{y}^{2}+B_{z}^{2})^{1/2}$ (black);
(e) kinetic energies of ions (blue) and electrons (red); and
(f) the ratio of ion to electron kinetic energies.
The shock front is located near the center of the plot, with the upstream region on the left and the downstream region on the right. A portion of the simulation domain is shown, spanning from $X/(c/\omega_{\rm pi})=-200$ in the upstream region to $X=0$ at the downstream boundary.
